 ## [Unreleased]
 
+## [0.4.0] - 2026-11-06
+
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now checks the model-supplied tool input against the tool's declared `inputSchema`
+  before the tool runs. A call the schema rejects returns a tool result describing what was wrong — the
+  property path and the expected type, never the offending values — so the model can correct the call on
+  its next round instead of your executor handling malformed input.
+- **Migration note:** a tool executor that used to hand-validate its input now receives only input the
+  declared schema accepts; a tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its own error message
+  stops seeing it. The check enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` only — extra properties still
+  reach the executor untouched, and nothing is coerced or defaulted. A static tool's schema compiles once
+  at `register`, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema fails at startup; registering through a
+  function resolves and checks the schema current at each call. The `Unknown tool: <name>` throw is
+  unchanged.
+
 ## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-17
 
 ### Changed
