+- Input reaching the executor has already passed the declared `inputSchema` (`required`, declared types, `enum`), so read fields directly -- a cast names the type, it does not defend against a missing value
+- Keys the schema does not declare may still be present -- validation does not inject `additionalProperties: false` -- so ignore what you did not declare
+- Input the schema rejects never reaches the executor: `ToolRegistry.execute` returns the rejection to the model as a tool result it can read and correct on its next call
 
 For tools that need to send messages directly to the client or suppress the AI's echo, return a `ToolResponse` object instead of a plain string. See [tool-responses.md](../specs/hal-engine-tool-responses/spec.md) for a full walkthrough.
 
